      "_id": "UAsZg2kQgJKrH0xo",
      "name": "Intoxicating Fruit (DC 14)",
      "type": "specialAbility",
      "img": "icons/svg/aura.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>The fruit of a dread tree produces a scent that is extremely intriguing to mammals. Any such creature within 100 feet of a dread tree must make a successful Will save (DC 10 + 1/2 the dread tree’s Hit Dice + its Charisma modifier) or move into its fighting space. Once there, the creature must make another successful Will save (same DC) or pick and eat the fruit. A creature too small to reach the branches eats fruit that has fallen from the tree. The fruit contains an ingested poison (Fortitude save DC 18; 1d6 Dex/unconsciousness for 2d6 rounds). The toxin remains viable for 1d6 days after picking.</p>",
        "source": "d20 Modern SRD",
        "srdUrl": "https://spellbooksoftware.com/d20mrsd/menacecreat1.html",
        "abilityType": "extraordinary",
        "sense": false,
        "activities": {
          "save": {
            "type": "save",
            "name": "Intoxicating Fruit",
            "actionType": "varies",
            "save": {
              "ability": "will",
              "calculation": "flat",
              "dc": 14,
              "onSuccess": "negate"
            }
          }
